{
  "email": "mei.chen@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports Excel shows Unlicensed Product; checking account status and sign-in state per KB-026."
}

{
  "user_id": 9,
  "reason": "Confirm recent sign-ins succeed with company account (KB-026 quick check) before deciding on license escalation."
}

{
  "summary": "User Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, device BL-LT-0109) reports Excel shows \"Unlicensed Product\" and editing is restricted. Checks: account active, not blocked, no failed logins, no password or lockout issues. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days show successful M365 sign-ins from the corporate network and successful VPN sign-ins with Duo push MFA, with no failures. Per KB-026, the user signs in correctly and still sees Unlicensed Product, which suggests the Microsoft 365 license may not be assigned. Please verify the E5/E3 or Office license assignment for this account. Also note the mailbox is at 99.4% use (50,890 MB of 51,200 MB), which may be relevant to license or service health and should be reviewed. Steps already done from KB-026: sign-in verification. Not yet done on the laptop: sign-out and reopen of Office apps, Office repair (KB-028). Tier 2 may want to run these with the user if the license check is clean.",
  "reason": "User signs in successfully but Excel still shows Unlicensed Product, which KB-026's escalation criteria covers (likely license not assigned)."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active and you are signing in normally, so the problem is most likely that Excel's Office license is not assigned to your account. I've passed this to our second-level team to check the license assignment. They may contact you to run a couple of quick steps on your laptop. Your mailbox is also almost full (about 99%), so you may want to clear some space while we look into this.",
  "internal_note": "User Mei Chen (user_id 9, device BL-LT-0109). Account active, not blocked, 0 failed logins, password set 2026-09-11, no lockout. Sign-in logs for the last 14 days: all 10 sign-ins succeeded (M365 from corporate network, VPN from residential with Duo push), no MFA denials. Per KB-026, a user who signs in correctly but still sees Unlicensed Product should be escalated, so I did that (escalation_id 1). Tier 2 should verify the M365 license assignment. Not yet tried on the laptop: sign out and reopen Office, and Office Quick Repair from KB-028. Side finding: mailbox is at 99.4% (50,890/51,200 MB), which should be reviewed. No actions were queued and no passwords were involved.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-026",
    "KB-028"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
